LAB – Fundamental Data Structure
Dr. Fei Zuo


Lab_2 FantasyBattle.cpp

OBJECTIVE:

	Develop a three-tier class inheritance system using public inheritance and dynamic binding.

Method:
	The parent class, Character, has been created as an abstract class and has two child classes, 
    Hero and Villain. These two classes each of a set of sub classes that inherit all the public 
    members of their parent class and grandparent class. 
	The Character abstract class defines name, health, level and has the virtual void function 
    displayInfo() = 0. Functions in Character have been created to give access to name, health, 
    and level to the sub classes:
        Character::setName(string)
        Character::setHealth(int)
        Character::setLevel(int)

    Each subclass overrides displayInfo() to display specific characteristics of itself and inherits 
    name, health, level. 

Dynamic Binding:

	As instructed in the assignment template, dynamic binding was used to assign the subclasses to 
    a Character pointer and then a for loop is used to iterate over the array and print the displayInfo() 
    function displaying all characteristics of each object. 

makefile:

    A makefile has been included with the following predefined commands:	
            run: compile and execute the a.exe file	
            clean: delete previous build	
            cleanRun: delete previous build, compile, and execute the a.exe file

